    {
      "anchor": "metadata",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Metadata"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "metadata",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "It is possible to add arbitrary key-value data to a VLAN definition. See Objects’ metadata field for more information."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "deleting",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Deleting"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "deleting",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "Not applicable - The VLAN will disappear when the subscription for it expires."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "attaching-to-servers",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Attaching To servers"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "attaching-to-servers",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "A VLAN can be attached to multiple servers. See Server Network Interfaces for more information on using VLANs in NIC configurations."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ips",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "IPs"
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ips",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "The IP object, contains the actual IP in it’s uuid attribute."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ips",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "The list of IPs includes the IPs that are owned (subscribed to) by the user, and the IPs which are dynamically assigned to user’s servers. The owned IP’s are differentiated by dynamically received IPs by the fact that they have a subscription attached to them (their subscription attribute is not empty)."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "ips",
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "The detailed listing includes more information about the IP object, such as netmask, nameservers, and gateway which will be set on the NIC. The netmask value is in CIDR notation (/24 for a 255.255.255.0 mask). The nameservers attribute contains a list of DNS servers, which will be assigned through DHCP, and the gateway attribute contains the IP of the default gateway for the current IP."
    },
